e_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saint Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1247758-the-mokteshaf-al-nour-what-is-the-name-of-this-group-in-arabic-spelling?p=1248201#post1248201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would I pronounce that?</div> </div> </div> </div>What? \u0645\u064f\u0643\u0652\u062a\u064e\u0634\u0650\u0641 \u0627\u0644\u0646\u064f\u0648\u0631?<br /> <br /> It is pronounced... let me see... muk (like mook) ta (like tax minus the -x) SHIF (like shift minus the -t; this syllable is stressed) / an (like an) NOOR (similar to noon, but ending with a rolled -r like in Spanish or Scottish English. Oh, and stressed)<br /> <br /> muk-ta-SHIF an-NOOR","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;No, no, don't look any further, my profile is actually more handsome than me&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3586-alqamar-alaswad","name":"Alqamar Alaswad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-20T14:21:20-07:00","id":1248213,"title":"","content":"... Thanks! ^^ I have the Natural Linguist merit and like to know this sort of stuff. ^^ How to you spell and pronounce proper Arabic for <i>Sebel-el-Mafouh Whash</i> or &quot;Path of Voracious Beast&quot; grimoire mentioned in Infernalism Path of Screams?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1973-saint-michael","name":"Saint Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1973_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-20T18:17:58-07:00","id":1248265,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mindszenty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1247758-the-mokteshaf-al-nour-what-is-the-name-of-this-group-in-arabic-spelling?p=1248002#post1248002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">UPD: I am not speaker of Arabic, but I guess the correct translation for \u201cThe discoverers of The Light\u201d would be something like <i>(al)muktashifun/muktashifin al-Nour</i>. The plural ending and first article are clearly missing from the original translation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, IIRC, they were originally mentioned in Mage: The Sorcerers' Crusade timeline, and since this was about 20 years ago, when the Internet was still in it's relatively early stages, translation issues were sometimes wonky unless the author or developer was fortunate enough to be or to know a fluent speaker of the language. And even then, you might end up with different answers from different people, depending on variables.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-20T22:05:46-07:00","id":1248319,"title":"","content":"I guess Sebel-al-Mafouh Whash is meant to represent Sabeel al-(<i>???)</i> Wahsh, &quot;Path or Way of the (Something) Beast&quot;.<br /> <br /> The only word that sounds similar to Mafouh is mufawwah, \u0645\u064f\u0641\u064e\u0648\u0651\u064e\u0647 . The problem is mufawwah means &quot;eloquent&quot;, not &quot;voracious&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;No, no, don't look any further, my profile is actually more handsome than me&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3586-alqamar-alaswad","name":"Alqamar Alaswad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-21T17:06:50-07:00","id":1248569,"title":"","content":"What's the proper word for &quot;voracious&quot; then? Do you know?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1973-saint-michael","name":"Saint Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1973_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-0